# R5-3b (steps/array-receiver-20261011.md, "R5-3b/R5-4, design before code"): a path is a root and a list of steps -- named
# fields and unnamed index expressions, each resolved against the current typed operand, `\[` continuing from the
# selected value (R5-G3).  `a[1]\[0]: 5` and `a[1]\[2]: 6` select cells of the row stored in a[1]; the row sees the
# writes; `length(a[1])` is the selected level's length.  The adjacent `a[1][2]` is the flat rectangular index of ONE
# Array (the book, semantics 116/1030; Codex CODEX-ARRAY-GROUPS-20261011-184637), not this: unit_steps_flat_refused.  Before: "own array index requires a supported integer
# expression" at the store, "root operation not walkable yet: this expression" at the read.  Natively and with the
# methods walked.  Entry 7.
fn: work () int
    []: []: int a 2
    []: int row 3
    a[1]: row
    a[1]\[0]: 5
    a[1]\[2]: 6
    if: row[0] != 5 || row[2] != 6
        return: 81
    if: a[1]\[0] != 5 || a[1]\[2] != 6 || a[1]\[0] != a[1]\[0]
        return: 82
    if: length(a[1]) != 3U || length(a) != 2U
        return: 83
    return: 7
end: work
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: work(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
